\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 -4: THB Up After Censure Motion Defeated \b0\par\par\uc2 337 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 10:33\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Among Asia's other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the Thai baht\par rose in reaction to the weekend's emphatic defeat of an\par opposition motion of no-confidence in the government of Thai\par prime minister Chuan Leekpai.\par    With the opposition barred from submitting another\par no-confidence motion for the next eight months, traders are\par looking for the baht to strengthen further from current\par levels.\par    At 0915 GMT (4:15 a.m. EST), the U.S. dollar was quoted\par at 38.70 baht (THB), down from THB39.3750 toward the close\par of Asian trading on Friday.\par    The Singapore dollar also gained against the U.S.\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , although sales of the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Singapore\par banks led traders to speculate that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the island republic's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par was \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market to cap excessive appreciation.\par    Late in Asia the U.S. dollar had broken through key\par support at S$1.60 to reach S$1.5995, down from S$1.6074 late\par in Asia on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    On the Philippine Dealing System, the peso recovered\par late in the day to finish slightly higher against the U.S.\par dollar in the first day of trading following the scrapping\par last week of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's permitted intraday volatility\par limits.\par    At the close of trading, the U.S. dollar was quoted at\par 37.690 pesos (PHP) down from PHP37.855 at Friday's close.\par    In North Asia both the new Taiwan dollar and the won\par ended higher in line with the regional trend, boosted by\par portfolio inflows and exporters repatriating U.S. dollar\par revenues ahead of the end of the quarter.\par    At the end of domestic trading the U.S. dollar was at\par NT$32.763, down from NT$32.780 at Friday's close. The U.S.\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was also at 1,366 won (KRW), down sharply from\par KRW1,448 at the end of trading on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  03-23-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0433EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du3n00r5c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
