\par\par \b \uc2  No need to change Singapore dollar policy - govt. \b0\par\par\uc2 184 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, March 11 (Reuters) - Singapore Deputy Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong said on Wednesday the government saw no reason to change its policy on the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  "Our \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not on autopilot. There is a trade weight which we monitor, but we exercise judgement in deciding how closely to follow (it) over the short-term," Lee told parliament. \par \par \uc2  He was replying to parliamentary questions on whether Singapore would devalue the Singapore dollar due to the sharp depreciation of other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Southeast Asia. \par \par \uc2  "I don't see ourselves having to make major adjustments to our policy as a result of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements," he said. \par \par \uc2  Singapore's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  from time to time to adjust the value of the Singapore dollar on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  The government says its policy is mainly guided by the value of the Singapore dollar against a trade-weighted basket of international \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  - Singapore Newsroom (65) 870-3080; Fax (65) 776-8112 \par \par \uc2  - Email: singapore.newsroom@reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926du3b00f4c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
