\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar A Touch Higher In Choppy Pre-Budget Trade \b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 1998\par 08:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)-- The Singapore dollar is a touch higher in choppy afternoon trading on Friday, ahead of the presentation of the Singapore budget, scheduled to begin after 0800 GMT (5:00 a.m. EST). \par \par \uc2  In early trading the Singapore dollar rose strongly on budget optimism and renewed regional confidence, penetrating U.S. dollar resistance at S$1.6180 to test S$1.6000. \par \par \uc2  Failing to break though, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was then pushed lower by interbank traders attempting to execute a squeeze play ahead of the Asian lunch break, said traders. \par \par \uc2  A subsequent second try at the S$1.6100 level was curtailed after Deputy Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong told parliament that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , of which he is chairman, would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market from time to time. \par \par \uc2  The MAS, the island republic's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , seeks to maintain Singapore dollar stability against an undisclosed trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The market interpreted the statement as a warning that the MAS is prepared to take action to prevent excessive Singapore dollar strengthening, and rushed to cover short U.S. dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  From being short U.S. dollars earlier, 'the market is now comfortably long,' according to a trader at a Singapore bank. \par \par \uc2  At 0700 GMT (2:00 a.m. EST) the U.S. dollar is trading at S$1.6200, a little lower than S$1.6235 late in Asian trading hours on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  At this level, say traders, the market is pricing modest corporate tax cuts into the budget. No drastic moves are expected for the remainder of the session. \par \par \uc2  In the local money market, overnight rates on Singapore dollar deposits are quoted at 0.75%-1.00%, down from 1.25%-1.50 earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  The three month interbank rate is unchanged at 5.50%-5.75%. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 27-02-98 \par \par \uc2  0711GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du2r01qv3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
