\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  says MAS will  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  when necessary. \b0\par\par\uc2 152 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Feb 27 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  will maintain confidence in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when necessary, Deputy Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Answering questions in parliament, Lee, who is also Chairman of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS), said "the MAS will maintain confidence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when necessary". \par \par \uc2  Lee also said fears of a sharp fall in the Indonesia rupiah dragging down the Singapore dollar were at this stage hypothetical and "the weight of the rupiah in our basket is small". \par \par \uc2  "The Indonesian government has not yet decided on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system," Lee said, referring to proposals to lock the value of the rupiah to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  -- Singapore Newsroom (65) 870-3080; Fax (65) 776-8112 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: singapore.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926du2r00yyj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
