\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Hopes of G7  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  lift Asia  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Angela Tan \par \uc2 677 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Februar 1998\par 07:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Feb 19 (Reuters) - The fate of Indonesia and its neighbours rests solely on this weekend's meeting of finance ministers and central bankers from the Group of Seven (G7) nations, dealers said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mostly firmer on strong hopes the G7 would issue a communique announcing a concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the beleaguered Asian units. \par \par \uc2  The communique is also expected to include a rupiah-stabilising alternative to Indonesia's proposed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, which had been under heavy international criticisms. \par \par \uc2  "There is an optimism at large that the G7 will come out with strong measures to resolve Asia's crisis and this has to, must, include an alternative to Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board," said a senior dealer with a European bank. \par \par \uc2  "Because if they do not, and Indonesia goes, Asia will be destabilised and we will head for a global recession," he said. \par \par \uc2  This G7 hope was fuelled by a Japanese report that there would be an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a measure advocated by Japan and aimed at restoring confidence in Asia and notably the rupiah, which had lost over 70 percent of its value. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the rupiah was firmer, hitting a high of 8,600 as confusion reigned over its planned \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system. \par \par \uc2  "The rupiah bearishness has been capped at 10,000 over the last few days because no one wants to short rupiah at this level in case the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board is implemented," said a dealer with a local bank. \par \par \uc2  "There is still a lot of nervousness over Suharto's intentions although it now appears more likely the proposal might have to be shelved," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia faces mounting international pressure on its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board proposal. \par \par \uc2  Singapore's Straits Times newspaper said on Thursday it should abandon plans for the board. \par \par \uc2  German Finance Minister Theo Waigel told a news conference in Jakarta that Indonesia did not presently fulfill the criteria for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board and that there was not an alternative to the International Monetary Fund (IMF) reforms. \par \par \uc2  Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed in tandem with the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian ringgit strengthened to 3.7200/7500 on offshore demand as players scrambled to sell the greenback. \par \par \uc2  "There is strong selling in the dollar/Malay. Stop losses were triggered at 3.75 and good interest to buy the ringgit at 3.71 to 3.73 by two major American players," said the senior dealer with a European bank. \par \par \uc2  The sale of dollar/Malay triggered sales in dollar/Sing. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Sing dollar was very likely to test 1.6200 when London starts trading later Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "There is a lot of squaring of dollar positions ahead of the G7. The threat of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is very real now," said a dealer. \par \par \uc2  "If 1.62 is broken, the Sing dollar could look to test 1.60/65. And that is very possible," he said. \par \par \uc2  Earlier on Thursday, Singapore's Deputy Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong said if the Singapore dollar was widely held, it would be more vulnerable to speculative attacks even though Singapore could fend this off with its huge reserves. \par \par \uc2  "As a small and open economy, we can't afford this," Lee told parliament. \par \par \uc2  He said the government was reviewing specific adjustments to the use of the Singapore dollar, particularly in the capital markets. \par \par \uc2  Fund selling ahead of the G7 gave the Thai baht a boost to 44.00/200 compared to 45.25/45.55 on late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Reports of Waigel saying the baht's current level did not reflect its true fundamentals also lifted the baht, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan dollar got an added boost from a soaring stock market, which mirrored Wall Street's record close on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  South Korean won was unchanged as dollar unwinding limits the dollar's rise. \par \par \uc2  Bucking the regional trend was the Hong Kong dollar as the sharp drop in local interest rates following the release of a better-than-expected fiscal 1998/99 budget proposals. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926du2j01fd7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
