\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore MAS Director: Peg To U.S. Dlr Would Be Dangerous \b0\par\par\uc2 118 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 1998\par 05:06\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Responding to a newspaper article, a director at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore said the Singapore dollar's credibility would be threatened if it were pegged to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  In a letter to the editor in Friday's Business Times, Khor Hoe Ee, MAS Economics Department director, said the wrong peg to the dollar would make Singapore 'a sitting duck for speculators.' \par \par \uc2  Instead, MAS, the country's effective \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , manages the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  'when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diverges from its long-term fundamentals,' Khor wrote. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 23-01-98 \par \par \uc2  0406GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du1n00mgk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
