\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Higher Late; Rally Follows Early Fall \b0\par\par\uc2 332 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 1998\par 10:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)-- The Singapore dollar is a touch higher against the U.S. dollar in late Asian trading on Thursday, compared to its level late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  After sliding abruptly in early trading in parallel to the dizzying fall in value of the rupiah, the Singapore dollar rallied in afternoon trading on profit-taking against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and on buying against the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  At 0850 GMT (3:50 a.m. EST) the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.7595, down from S$1.7604 in late trading on Wednesday, and well below Thursday's intraday high of S$1.7680. \par \par \uc2  'People took profits below S$1.77. They were a bit afraid that something was cooking and that the central banks would come in with concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' said a trader at a \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  bank. \par \par \uc2  In November the Bank of Japan and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , acting in concert with Bank Indonesia, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by selling U.S. dollars against the rupiah to prop up the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Although the effect of the rupiah action was short-lived, it also had the effect of bolstering other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the U.S. dollar, as traders and investors were caught long on the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar was also strengthened by purchases of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the ringgit, according to traders. \par \par \uc2  At 0850 GMT (3:50 a.m. EST) the ringgit is quoted at S$0.3900, down from S$0.4101 late on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In the domestic money market, the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits is at 0.25%-0.375%, down from 1.0%-1.25% earlier and 0.25%-0.50% late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The three-month interbank rate is at 7.0%-8.0%, from 8.75%-9.25% and 8.5%-9.5%. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 22-01-98 \par \par \uc2  0905GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du1m00k7k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
