\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Down Vs U.S. Dollar, But Up Vs Ringgit \b0\par\par\uc2 319 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 1998\par 03:50\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is down against the U.S. dollar in early trading on Thursday, in reaction to the rupiah's free-fall against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar's slide against the U.S. dollar has been checked, however, by renewed weakness in the ringgit, which has seen fresh selling against Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 0230 GMT (9:30 PM Wednesday EST) the U.S. dollar is trading at S$1.7660, up from S$1.7604 in late Asian trading on Wednesday, but below its intraday high seen earlier Thursday of S$1.7670. \par \par \uc2  At the same time the ringgit is trading at S$0.3882, down from S$0.3960 late Wednesday, as the U.S. dollar has risen to MYR4.52 from MYR4.45. \par \par \uc2  'The Singapore dollar is weak, but the ringgit is weaker, and that is supporting the Singapore dollar for the time being,' said a senior trader at a Singapore bank. \par \par \uc2  At the same time market participants are nervous of selling the Singapore dollar down too far or too fast, given the danger of commercial U.S. dollar sales and the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In recent days, big sellers of U.S. dollars have emerged at S$1.77, and market participants are wary of approaching that level again for fear of triggering further sales. \par \par \uc2  In the domestic money market, the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits is at 1.0%-1.25%, compared with 0.25%-0.50% late Wednesday and 2.0%-2.5% earlier Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The three-month interbank rate is at 8.75%-9.25%, from 8.5%-9.5% and 8.0%-9.0%. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800; \par \par \uc2  tom.holland@djmarkets.com.sg \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 22-01-98 \par \par \uc2  0250GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du1m00jb8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
