\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Up Early, Seen In Range Amid Cautious Mkt \b0\par\par\uc2 243 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 1998\par 03:41\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is holding steady near S$1.7900 to the U.S. dollar early Tuesday as the market watches cautiously a parade of top-level officials tour through Southeast Asia. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Singapore dollar's movements appear capped at about S$1.8000 to the dollar, with U.S. dollar buyers appearing around S$1.7850. \par \par \uc2  The market is watching carefully U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers and International Monetary Fund Managing Director Michel Camdessus, among others, who are touring the region this week to hold talks on the ongoing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  turmoil. \par \par \uc2  About 0230 GMT (9:30 p.m. EST Monday), the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.7895, down from S$1.8005 in late trading in Singapore Monday. \par \par \uc2  Also, rumors in the market suggest the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the country's effective \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the money market to cool interest rates, which had spiked in tandem with the renewed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness last week. \par \par \uc2  In the local money market, the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits was quoted at 6.000%-7.000%, up from 5.500%-6.000% late Monday in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  The three-month interbank rate was at 9.000%-11.000%, from 8.000%-10.000%. \par \par \uc2  -By Roger Malone; 65-421-4800; rmalone@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 13-01-98 \par \par \uc2  0241GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \