\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  -2: Singapore Dlr Lower As Stk Mkt Hit \b0\par\par\uc2 285 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 1998\par 12:39\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The rupiah's weakness was credited by some market\par participants for the Singapore dollar's fall on Monday. The\par Singapore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell, with the U.S. dollar climbing to\par end Asian hours at S$1.8005, up from S$1.7750 at the close\par of trading on Friday.\par    The Singapore dollar's drop came as the republic's\par benchmark Straits Times stock index plunged by 8.75%,\par impelled partly by fears over the extent of Singapore banks'\par exposure to Indonesian credit. Those fears were further\par heightened in late trading by the announcement that Keppel\par Bank and Tat Lee Bank, two of Singapore's weaker banks, are\par to merge.\par    "We are seeing genuine fund interest to buy (U.S.)\par dollars," against the Singapore dollar, said a trader at a\par U.S. bank in the republic. The buying interest was partially\par offset by U.S. dollar sales at the S$1.80 level by local\par banks, which prompted some traders to suspect \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the country's de\par facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Elsewhere in the region the announcement that the\par Malaysian government is to permit the perceived bail-out of\par the troubled Renong Group by subsidiary United Engineers\par Malaysia depressed the ringgit in early trading.\par Profit-taking by offshore funds limited the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's fall,\par however.\par    "Fundamentally the ringgit should be lower, and we will\par see it drop further when this profit-taking is over," said\par the U.S. bank trader.\par    At the close of Asian trading the U.S. dollar was quoted\par at 4.6800 ringgit (MYR), up from MYR4.6540 on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  01-12-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0639EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020020317du1c0042z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
