\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Higher Early; Overnight Low Of S$1.8144/Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 273 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 1998\par 04:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is slightly higher against the U.S. dollar in early Asian dealings Friday compared with late Thursday, but traders expect further losses in the short term. \par \par \uc2  Market players expect the U.S. dollar to break above S$1.80 in the short term but said current resistance stems from fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the country's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar touched an overnight high of S$1.8144. \par \par \uc2  Collapsing domestic stock prices and spillover of negative sentiment from the region into Singapore are key factors for the further downside, market players said. The benchmark Straits Times Industrial Index is down 107.71 points, or 8.5%, to 1162.99 points early Friday and is the second biggest loser in the region after the Philippines. \par \par \uc2  The short-term target for the U.S. dollar, when it convincingly breaches above S$1.80, is between S$1.85 and S$1.90, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0240 GMT (9:40 p.m. EST), the dollar is trading around S$1.7810, up from S$1.7740 from 0000 GMT early in Asian trading but down from S$1.7895 in late Thursday dealings. \par \par \uc2  In the local money market, the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits was quoted at 25.000%-30.000%, up from 15.000%-25.000% late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The three-month interbank rate was at 12.000%-14.000%, up from 10.000%-12.000%. \par \par \uc2  -Joseph Rajendran; 65-421-4800. \par \par \uc2  (END) Do