\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Crisis/Glance-2:Indonesia Rupiah At New All-Time Low \b0\par\par\uc2 264 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 1998\par 15:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  --The Indonesian rupiah continued to drop, falling through IDR10,000 to the dollar to IDR10,550, as worries mounted that Indonesian companies won't be able to pay off their short-term debts. \par \par \uc2  Investors are pulling out of Indonesian stocks, with the market index down nearly 12% Thursday to a four-year low. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said the second tranche of the IMF bailout package is being 'processed,' and said the bank will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  --The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Hong Kong stock markets have borne the brunt Thursday of their neighbors' economic troubles. Singapore's benchmark stock index is down 7%, near a 5 1/2-year low. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong's Hang Seng index fell 3%, one day after diving 6%, with local interbank rates rising on banks' reluctance to lend in the region. Investors are worried about the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ability to maintain the Hong Kong dollar's peg to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The drop in Hong Kong shares again pulled Shanghai and Shenzhen shares down with them. \par \par \uc2  --The dollar rose versus the yen after Japanese Vice Finance Minister Sakakibara and U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Summers did not threaten joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to support the yen, in the wake of their meeting in Washington. \par \par \uc2  --South Korea and the IMF agreed to revisions in the nation's economic projections, and President Kim Dae-Jung reconfirmed South Korea would honor the bailout agreement. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 08-01-98 \par \par \uc2  1413GMT \par \par \uc2  1042 4190 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du18005va\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
