\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr/Late -2: Speed, Not Level, Seen Worrying MAS \b0\par\par\uc2 230 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 1998\par 10:50\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  About midday, MAS, the country's effective \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , warned it would take 'decisive' action against speculative attacks targeting its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , reminding the market that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  occasionally 'to ensure orderly movements' on the market. \par \par \uc2  But the authority noted its policy doesn't focus on 'any single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' but rather a trade-weighted basket. In this regard, the Singapore dollar has remained stable, 'notwithstanding the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  turmoil,' it added. \par \par \uc2  'MAS would carry more weight than the other central banks because it has the ability to act,' said one dealer in Singapore. 'But at the end of the day, I would think that their concern is not so much the right value for the Singapore dollar, but the speed at which it is depreciating.' \par \par \uc2  While the MAS statement may have reminded market participants that they're being watched, exchange rates remained stable immediately after the statement was released. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar turned higher only after the Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In the local money market, the overnight rate on \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar deposits was quoted at 10.000%-11.000%, from 5.000%-5.500% earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  The 3-month interbank rate was at 9.500%-10.500%, from 8.000%-8.500%. \par \par \uc2  -By Roger Malone; 65-421-4800; rmalone@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswire