\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore MAS/Comments/Analysts -2: Sort Of Moral Suasion \b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 1998\par 09:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Earlier, as reported, the MAS, the country's effective \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Wednesday it's ready to stop any speculative attacks against the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar. \par \par \uc2  MAS said in the statement that it occasionally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets 'to ensure the orderly movement' of the Singapore dollar exchange rate consistent with its policy and economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  'We do not publicize our exchange rate \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' it said, but warned, 'The MAS stands ready to act decisively against any speculative attack on the Singapore dollar.' \par \par \uc2  Commenting on the statement, Skandinaviska Enskilda Banken regional economist Chia Woon Kien said, 'The contents (of the MAS statement) are not new but it is a message to the market that the MAS isn't sleeping. A lot of other (regional) central banks appear to be quiet.' \par \par \uc2  'The (MAS) message just underscores Singapore's macroeconomic policy. But it's sort of a moral suasion to the market that maybe the Singapore dollar has risen too fast in too short a period,' said a regional economist at a major U.S. investment bank here. \par \par \uc2  Economists also said that the MAS statement also showed that the de facto central is trying to find the appropriate approach to reminding the market about its macroeconomic policies, given that it generally keeps a low profile. \par \par \uc2  At a time when most central banks in the region lack the funds to support their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  or the stamina to defend them, the MAS' comments appear to err on the side of caution while at the same time attempting to deliver its message, economists added. \par \par \uc2  Rising domestic interest rates could have been another key factor in motivating the MAS statement Wednesday, said one economist. The continued rise in the U.S. dollar against the Singapore dollar is likely to exert an upward pressure on interbank money market rates, eventually resulting in higher domestic lending rates and braking economic growth, he said. \par \par \uc2  Key interest rates have already been hiked twice in the past month. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 07-01-98 \par \par \uc2  0834GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du170041g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
