\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  -2: MAS Midday Comments Set Stage \b0\par\par\uc2 232 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 1998\par 12:20\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    About 1100 GMT (6:00 a.m. EST), the U.S. dollar was\par trading at MYR4.5755, down from a record high of MYR4.8800\par earlier in the day, but up from MYR4.3400 in late Asian\par trading Tuesday.\par    Setting the stage for Anwar's remarks and Bank Negara\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the\par country's effective \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , warned on Wednesday it\par "stands ready to act decisively against any speculative\par attack against the Singapore dollar."\par    MAS Managing Director Koh Yong Guan also reminded\par markets that the authority \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  "from time to time" in\par order to "ensure orderly movements" on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par    The Singapore dollar didn't react immediately to Koh's\par comments, but traders said they gave the market food for\par thought.\par    "MAS would carry more weight than the other central\par banks because it has the ability to act," said one dealer in\par Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  "But at the end of the day, I would think that\par their concern is not so much the right value for the\par Singapore dollar, but the speed at which it is\par depreciating."\par    In late trading, the U.S. dollar was at S$1.7529, down\par from an intraday high of S$1.7930, its highest level since\par late March 1991, but above S$1.7375 late Tuesday.\