\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Nervous Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  pull out of depths. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sonali Desai \par \uc2 1,053 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Jan 7 (Reuters) - Southeast Asia's ravaged \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  limped tentatively out of the depths in late Wednesday trade as fears of concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action halted a mad scramble for dollars. \par \par \uc2  Speculation Japan might ask the United States to help it prop up the sagging yen pushed the U.S. dollar below 133 yen ahead of a meeting between U.S. and Japanese monetary officials, injecting a note of caution in other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  "The market is actually quite worried there might be some concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the dollar/yen and that all the regional central banks will come in as well," a U.S. bank dealer in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Southeast Asia headed relentlessly lower due to heavy dollar demand from companies and investors amid poor liquidity and wide spreads. \par \par \uc2  "It's moving in big figures these days. I come in in the morning and don't recognise the levels. I go for lunch and the same thing happens," said one senior regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  The bloodletting on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets spilled over, yet again, into Asian bourses and several stock indices fell through key support levels. Oil markets and many commodities were also savaged by the rapid fall of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But the Malaysian ringgit recovered in late trade as players liquidated long dollar positions after Finance Minister Anwar Ibrahim confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to defend the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  It was at 4.5600/700 at 1100 GMT after falling to a low of 4.8800 in morning trade. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Bank Negara Malaysia had sold dollars for ringgit at various levels. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement that Malaysia's total debt amounted to $45.2 billion or 42 percent of its Gross Domestic Product. \par \par \uc2  It said short-term debt at the end of June accounted for 30 percent of total external debt outstanding, in contrast with a ratio published by the Bank of International Settlements of 56 percent, which had earlier spooked the market. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar was also sharply higher at 1.7500/50 to the U.S. dollar after falling to a more than seven-year low of 1.7940 earlier. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS), the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sharp drop. \par \par \uc2  The MAS said in a written response to questions from Reuters that it stood ready to "act decisively against any speculative attack on the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar". \par \par \uc2  "The MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market from time to time to ensure orderly movements of the Sing dollar exchange rate ... We do not publicise our exchange rate \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," MAS managing director Koh Yong Guan said in the statement. \par \par \uc2  Late rumours that the MAS had asked \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders in certain banks work to late on Wednesday also spurred some short-covering in the Singapore dollar, dealers said. The MAS declined comment. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah perked up a bit to 7,900/8,000 to the dollar from an early low of 8,450, but dealers said it remained shaky amid disappointment over Indonesia's 1998/99 budget, unveiled on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said Jakarta's projections of four percent economic growth, inflation at nine percent, the rupiah at 4,000 to the dollar and an increase in tax revenue would be difficult to achieve given the depth of Indonesia's crisis. \par \par \uc2  A Washington Post report that International Monetary Fund officials had called Indonesia's economic crisis worrisome and faulted Jakarta for failing to follow through on pledges to restructure the economy also dented the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht recovered from below the 53.00 level to the dollar in domestic and offshore markets in late trade after Finance Minister Tarrin Nimmanahaeminda said the government would announce new measures to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The baht was at 52.85/53.15 to the dollar onshore against 53.10/30 six hours earlier and 52.05/35 late on Tuesday. The offshore rate was at 52.50/53.00 against 54.10/30 earlier. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso ended weak at 45.35 to the dollar but off its opening low of 46.50. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the overnight borrowing rate to 12 percent from 11 percent in a bid to curb speculation. \par \par \uc2  Manila traders said the rate hike had little impact, but the peso received some support from a plan under which commercial banks would offer non-deliverable forwards from 0500 GMT. \par \par \uc2  This will help companies hedge dollar-denominated debts against further falls in the peso without having to buy dollars now. \par \par \uc2  North Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to look jaundiced with the Taiwan dollar faring the worst. \par \par \uc2  It fell through a 10-year support of T$34 to the U.S. dollar within minutes of opening and ended at T$34.400 against Tuesday's T$33.755 close in the face of mayhem elsewhere in Asia. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the previously stolid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to head for the T$35 level unless other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  saw a sustained rebound. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan announced a rare trade deficit of US$80.1 million for December, reflecting civilian aircraft imports, against a surplus of US$1.078 billion in December 1996, the Finance Ministry said. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar clung to the 7.75 support level against the U.S. dollar and forwards jumped amid jitters in other \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen offering short-dated funds to ease rates in an effort to boost the sagging stock market. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won was relatively unscathed but fell off its highs of 1,680 to the dollar as expectations of importer dollar demand near the 1,600 level eclipsed foreign fund inflows to the stock market. \par \par \uc2  It ended at 1,745 to the dollar against Tuesday's 1,742 close. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar ploughed 11-year-lows, weakening to US$0.6316, before rebounding to 0.6372/77 from 0.6345/50 late on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The New Zealand dollar also recovered to US$0.5680/87 against 0.5622/29 six hours earlier. \par \par \uc2  -- Singapore newsroom (65) 870-3080 Fax (65) 776-8112 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: singapore.newsroomzreuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0