\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore dollar traded at a low of 1.7850. \b0\par\par\uc2 211 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Jan 7 (Reuters) - The U.S. dollar continued its beating of some Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , sending the Singapore dollar trading to a low of 1.7850 early on Wednesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Sentiment stays weak and the weaker regionals are not helping. They will inevitably weigh on the Sing," said one dealer, referring to the free-fall of the Indonesian rupiah towards an unchartered territory of 8,000 level. \par \par \uc2  "It is likely to remain weak as we hear more about the difficulties some Asian countries will have in meeting the the International Monetary Fund bailout terms," he said. \par \par \uc2  At 0135 GMT, the Singapore dollar was quoted firmer at 1.7730/80 to the greenback. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's gains were capped by profit-taking orders when dollar/Sing hit 1.7850, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "There was a lot of interest, but today's spread is wider than the past few days. Moves tend to be exaggerated," said another dealer. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said it was unclear if Singapore's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS), \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  but noted the presence of several local banks. \par \par \uc2  -- Angela Tan (65) 870-3083; Fax (65) 776-8112 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: singapore.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926du17017kv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
