\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Late-AM: US$ Down;  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fears Cap Rise \b0\par\par\uc2 410 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 1998\par 04:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The U.S. dollar is slightly lower but expected to be steady in late-morning Singapore trading Monday from levels around 0215 GMT in Tokyo, amid moderate volumes. \par \par \uc2  Although market players in Singapore are upbeat about the prospects for the dollar, most fear that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will cap the U.S \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise, especially against the yen, for now. In addition, willingness by market players to take profits around Y132.50 is seen capping the dollar's rise, they said. \par \par \uc2  '\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems to be a concern and some comments this morning seem to have taken the sting out of the dollar (versus the yen),' said the chief dealer at a major European bank here. As reported earlier, Haruhiko Kuroda, head of the ministry's international finance bureau, told a group of reporters he 'doesn't accept' a further weakening of the yen. \par \par \uc2  A treasury economist at a U.K. bank here said the 'Bank of Japan's resolve to limit the yen's weakness' will cap the dollar's rise for the short term. The higher end resistance for the dollar is seen around Y133.30, said the economist. \par \par \uc2  Apart from fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said market players are ready to take profits if the dollar rallies. 'We're not sure is Europe or New York will want to take the dollar higher. They themselves want to lock in some of their profits around Y132.50,' said a senior dealer at a Japanese bank here. \par \par \uc2  Looking head, the dollar is seen well supported at Y129.70-.90 against the yen. Against the German \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar is seen holding between DM1.7970 and DM1.7820 for the rest of Asian dealings, said dealers. \par \par \uc2  Around 0255 GMT, the dollar is at Y132.29, down from Y132.40, quoted at both 0215 GMT and late Friday in New York. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is at 1.7974 marks, down from DM1.7995, and down from DM1.8045 in New York Friday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at $1.6435, a touch higher than $1.6433 at 0215 GMT and above from $1.6407 late Friday in New York. The mark is quoted at Y73.57, steady from Y73.58 around 0215 GMT, but up from Y73.37 in New York late Friday. \par \par \uc2  -By Joseph Rajendran; 65 421 4800. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 05-01-98 \par \par \uc2  0310GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du15002ac\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
