\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Lower Early, Hit By Regional Weakness \b0\par\par\uc2 227 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 1998\par 04:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is sharply lower against its U.S. counterpart early Monday, pulled down by general weakness in the region. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the U.S. dollar seems to have reached decisively above S$1.7000 in early trading Monday, with S$1.7100-S$1.7150 watched as the next target. \par \par \uc2  'Customers are buying whenever there's a dip,' said one trader at an Asian bank in Singapore. 'The Singapore dollar can't be immune from the regional weakness.' \par \par \uc2  About 0300 GMT (10 p.m. EST Sunday), the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading at S$1.7055, up from S$1.6955 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said Bank Negara, the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was buying ringgit early Monday when the U.S. dollar breached 4.0200 ringgit, giving the ringgit and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar a brief reprieve. \par \par \uc2  But soon after the reported \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , both \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  had retraced most of the ground gained. \par \par \uc2  In the local money market, the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits was quoted at 1.250%-1.500%, down from 2.250%-2.500% late Friday. The 3-month interbank rate was at 6.500%-6.750%, down from 6.625%-6.875%. \par \par \uc2  By Roger Malone; 65-421-4800; rmalone@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 05-01-98 \par \par \uc2  0303GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du150029z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
