\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Lower Early Vs U.S. Dlr, Seen Breaking S$1.70 \b0\par\par\uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Januar 1998\par 03:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is weaker against the U.S. dollar in early Asian trading Friday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  braces for another push lower. \par \par \uc2  About 0200 GMT (9 p.m. EST Thursday), the U.S. dollar was trading at S$1.6910, up from S$1.6845 in late Asian trading Wednesday. The market was closed for the New Year's Day holiday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they expect the dollar to test above S$1.7000 again during Friday's session, with one citing a short-term target as high as S$1.8000. \par \par \uc2  The dealers noted overall negative sentiment for Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , emphasizing the Singapore dollar's drop against the U.S. dollar has lagged behind that of its sibling \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In his new year message released Wednesday, Singapore Prime Minister Goh Chok Tong warned 1998 will be 'a more difficult year' for the economy than 1997. He also noted the Singapore dollar's decline since July 1 has been less than half that of the Philippine peso, the Malaysia ringgit, the Thai baht and the Indonesian rupiah. \par \par \uc2  But unless there's a exaggerated move on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, traders said its unlikely that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the country's effective \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect the S$1.7000 level. \par \par \uc2  'I don't think MAS will come in, ... (particularly) if you look at the other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region,' said one trader at a bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  He said the U.S. dollar should trade in a range of S$1.700-S$1.7500 during the Asian session Friday. It last poked above S$1.7000 Dec. 17. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 02-01-98 \par \par \uc2  0227GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du12000bb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
