\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 :  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Aids Rupiah; Others Steady \b0\par\par\uc2  By Roger Malone \par \uc2 219 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Dezember 1997\par 10:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed a slight weakening bias amid very thin volume in after-Christmas trading Friday. \par \par \uc2  'Unless you're really desperate, I don't think there's much buying interest in this thin market when the spreads are really killers,' a trader at a bank in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  Sandwiched between Thursday's holiday in London and New York and Friday's holiday in London, the Asian session Friday was characterized by thin volume and little interest, traders said. \par \par \uc2  'I think we're set for the year, except for people who are buying for corporates,' said another dealer in Singapore. 'There is no interest, no trade.' \par \par \uc2  Although the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  garnered some support from the South Korean won early in the Asian session, the thin market made exchange rates subject to sharp fluctuations, participants said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said Bank Indonesia, the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , jumped into the market twice in late Asian trading to protect the rupiah after the U.S. dollar spiked above 6,000 rupiah. \par \par \uc2  About 0900 GMT, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at 5,300 rupiah, down from 5,950 rupiah early Friday in Asia and from 5,900 rupiah late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 26-12-97 \par \par \uc2  0912GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtcq09yod\par }