\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Down Late Vs U.S. Dlr; Seen In Tight Range \b0\par\par\uc2 306 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Dezember 1997\par 10:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (AP-Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is down against the U.S. dollar in late trading Monday, compared with its level at the end of Asian hours on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Throughout much of Monday's session, however, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has remained within a tight 50 point range, with little trading interest. \par \par \uc2  At 0920 GMT (4:20 a.m. EST) the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.6755, down from its early morning intraday high of S$1.6800, but above S$1.6654 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  In early trading, market participant's bought the dollar on expectations of continued Asian weakness, according to traders. The rally soon ran out of steam, however, as fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the republic's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , capped the rise at S$1.68. \par \par \uc2  Moody's Investors Service's mid-morning downgrading of Indonesian, Malaysian and Thai credit ratings had little effect on the Singapore dollar, said traders. Moody's confirmed Singapore's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt ceiling at Aa1. \par \par \uc2  With most market participants now having squared their positions ahead of the year's end, traders expect the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to remain in a S$1.67 to S$1.68 range for the rest of the week. \par \par \uc2  In the domestic money market, the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits is quoted at 5.00%-5.25% up from 4.500%-5.000% earlier in the session, and at the same level as late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The three-month interbank rate is at 7.500%-8.000%, unchanged from earlier Monday, and down from 8.000%-9.000% late Friday. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800; \par \par \uc2  tom.holland@djmarkets.com.sg) \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 22-12-97 \par \par \uc2  0938GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtcm09ue0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
