\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Late-AM: Dlr Edges Up Vs Yen After Early Fall \b0\par\par\uc2 323 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 1997\par 04:43\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (AP-Dow Jones)--The U.S. dollar is again edging higher against the Japanese yen in late-morning trading on Friday in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after earlier dropping on what traders said was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Japan. \par \par \uc2  At 0320 GMT (10:20 p.m. EST) the dollar is quoted at Y129.20, up from Y128.90 an hour ago in Tokyo and above Y128.73 in New York late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  After rising strongly in early trading, the dollar dropped sharply, forced down, said traders, by the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offering dollars at Y129.50. \par \par \uc2  Now the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is again edging higher as traders and investors seek to buy the dollar. \par \par \uc2  'Although there is some fear of more \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , overall the dollar is heading higher,' said a trader at a German bank in Singapore. The dollar's up trend is so strong, that, he said, that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has now regained more than half the ground it lost against the yen following the Bank of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  'It only has to rise one more big figure (100 points) before we are back up to where we were before Wednesday,' he said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's rise is being driven partly by traders and investors who shorted the dollar as it fell now buying to cover their positions, said traders. \par \par \uc2  Activity in other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is largely subdued, said traders. \par \par \uc2  Against the mark the dollar is quoted at DM1.7736, down from DM1.7742 earlier in Tokyo and below DM1.7745 late Thursday in New York. \par \par \uc2  The mark is at Y72.84, up from Y72.67 earlier in Tokyo and Y72.50 late Thursday in New York, as the mark shadows the dollar's rise against the yen. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland, Singapore AP-Dow Jones (65) 421-4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 19-12-97 \par \par \uc2  0343GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtcj09qyf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
