\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Up Early Vs U.S. Dlr; Calm Seen, Suharto Eyed \b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 1997\par 03:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (AP-Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is slightly stronger against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early Asian trading Thursday, with market participants expected a calm session with low volume. \par \par \uc2  But players said if Indonesian President Suharto fails to appear at a military cadet graduation in Jakarta Thursday morning, a strong bout of dollar buying could push the rupiah lower, bringing its regional siblings down with it. \par \par \uc2  'I see it quiet for most of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to a slight (U.S.) dollar strengthening,' a dealer at an Asian bank in Singapore said. Barring major news, he said the U.S. dollar should trade in a range of S$1.6730 to S$1.6850. \par \par \uc2  About 0200 GMT (9:00 p.m. EST), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.6672, down from S$1.6760 in late Asian trading Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  'The Singapore dollar is quiet, and we're not really expecting a lot,' said another \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Following market talk that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the country's effective \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday and Wednesday, no government action is expected Thursday unless the U.S. dollar starts racing toward S$1.6900. \par \par \uc2  'If there is renewed (U.S. dollar) buying out of fear or positioning, they may come in,' the trader at the Asian bank said. \par \par \uc2  In the local money market, the overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits was quoted at 5.000%-5.500%, down from 5.500%-6.000% late Wednesday in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  The three-month interbank rate was at 8.500%-9.000%, up from 8.000%-8.500% late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Roger Malone; 65-421-4800; rmalone@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 18-12-97 \par \par \uc2  0217GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtci09rhi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
