\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Higher Late On Ctrl Bk Action, US Dlr's Fall \b0\par\par\uc2 321 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 1997\par 10:47\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (AP-Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar is stronger against the U.S. dollar in late trading on Wednesday in response to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early trading and the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dramatic slide against the Japanese yen. \par \par \uc2  At 0920 GMT (4:20 a.m. EST) the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.6780, down from S$1.6995 at Wednesday's Asian open and S$1.6917 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In overnight trading on Tuesday, European and U.S. traders pushed the U.S. dollar to a six-year high of S$1.7180 after Singapore's prime minister, Goh Chok Tong, told Dow Jones that he was 'not unduly worried' by the recent 18% depreciation of the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  'The move was overdone, and that's why the MAS stepped in,' said a trader at a Japanese bank in Singapore, who estimated that the republic's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had spent around $200 million in U.S. dollars in the action. Other traders, however, said it was impossible to estimate the amount spent. \par \par \uc2  'The government is not against a weaker Singapore dollar, they just want to moderate the pace of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' said the Japanese bank trader. \par \par \uc2  Local money market rates have risen sharply on Wednesday afternoon, reflecting the continued downward pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate on Singapore dollar deposits is currently quoted at 5.50%-6.00%, up from 4.00%-4.50% earlier, but down from 6.25%-6.5% late Tuesday. The three-month interbank rate is at 8.00%-8.50%, up from 7.500%-8.000% earlier in the day and higher than 7.75%-7.875% late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland;65 421 4800;tom.holland@djmarkets.com.sg \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-12-97 \par \par \uc2  0947GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtch09oxw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
