\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore MAS says sees no reason for S$ to weaken. \b0\par\par\uc2 144 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Dec 17 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) said on Wednesday the country's economic fundamentals were strong and it saw no reason for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar to weaken. \par \par \uc2  "The MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market from time to time to iron out short-term fluctuations. We do not publicise our exchange rate \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the MAS said in a written response to questions from Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "As Singapore's economic fundamentals remain sound, we see no reason why the Singapore dollar should weaken," it said. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar firmed above the 1.68 level to the U.S. dollar on Wednesday, partly on talk the MAS had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar fell to a more than six year low of 1.7175 in thin London trade overnight. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtch00wcn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
