\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore dollar slide seen slowing. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sonali Desai \par \uc2 642 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Dec 17 (Reuters) - Apparent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support helped lift the Singapore dollar from six-year lows against the U.S. dollar on Wednesday, but dealers and analysts expected more weakness in the once sturdy \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  It firmed above the 1.68 level to the U.S. dollar, partly due to talk the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS), the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , had sold U.S. dollars above S$1.70 to stem the decline. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said MAS commments that it saw no reason for the Singapore dollar to weaken given the country's strong economic fundamentals further boosted the Singapore dollar to 1.6720/70 at 1005 GMT against 1.6935/55 late on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said the MAS had also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in thin London markets overnight when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar succumbed to mounting pressure and dived to a low of 1.7175 per U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The MAS was in in London last night. When dollar/Sing got to a high of 1.7175, they were in selling," said a senior regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader. \par \par \uc2  "I heard they were in again through some local banks this morning. But then again, other local banks were bidding on the other side," he said. \par \par \uc2  The previously stolid Singapore dollar had lost nearly seven percent in three trading days as market participants sold it on a perception that it needed to fall for Singapore exports to remain competitive regionally. \par \par \uc2  But the MAS's comments on Wednesday, and the yen's steep drop against the U.S. dollar, gave dealers cause to suspend their selling spree. \par \par \uc2  "As Singapore's economic fundamentals remain sound, we see no reason why the Singapore dollar should weaken," the MAS said in a written response to questions from Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "The MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market from time to time to iron out short-term fluctuations. We do not publicise our exchange rate \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," it said. \par \par \uc2  Singapore government officials have said previously during months of Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  turmoil that they were not concerned about the domestic dollar's slide against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the MAS comments highlighted Singapore's dilemma as a highly trade-dependent economy. \par \par \uc2  "I think they're a bit ambivalent, because on the one hand there's the real threat of competition from the closer exporter countries like Malaysia, Taiwan. On the other hand, they would be concerned about import inflation," said Chia Woon Khien, head of Asian research at Skandinaviska Enskilda Banken. \par \par \uc2  "And the bigger concern is the stability of the financial markets. Just like Hong Kong, they would not want a Sing dollar that's going to be spinning downwards because it would affect a lot of investment interests in this country," Chia said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers and analysts agreed there was a basis for the Singapore dollar to track declines in neighbouring \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though at a slower pace, in the short term. \par \par \uc2  "We expect more weakness. It's at current levels only because of MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said an analyst at a foreign bank who declined to be identified. \par \par \uc2  She said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was aimed more at smoothing moves in the exchange rate. "I don't think there is a level they're defending." \par \par \uc2  She said the Singapore dollar was likely to reach 1.75 to the U.S. dollar by March. \par \par \uc2  Most dealers expected the Singapore dollar to slide below the 1.70 level again in the weeks ahead. \par \par \uc2  "They (the MAS) were concerned because it moved so fast. But I don't think they'd mind if dollar/Sing moved slowly up to test 1.72, especially if the Malaysian ringgit goes back below 3.90," a U.S. bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  -- Singapore Newsroom (65) 870-3080; Fax (65) 776-8112 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: singapore.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtch00w3z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
