\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Broadly Stronger As Dlr Tumbles Vs Yen \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tom Holland \par \uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 1997\par 13:05\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Southeast Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par enjoyed a break from their recent hammering on Tuesday. The\par U.S. dollar's five yen tumble against the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par during Asian hours eased pressure throughout the region,\par allowing Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to end broadly flat to higher\par against the U.S. dollar.\par    The biggest climber was the Singapore dollar.\par    Late Tuesday, Singapore's prime minister, Goh Chok Tong,\par told Dow Jones that he was "not unduly worried" by the\par Singapore dollar's 18% depreciation since the end of 1996.\par In response, European and U.S. players pushed the Singapore\par dollar to a six-year low of S$1.7180 during overnight\par trading.\par    The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rebounded strongly in early trading on\par Wednesday, however, as traders said that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary\par Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore entered the market, selling U.S.\par dollars to check the Singapore dollar's fall.\par    "The move was overdone, and that's why the MAS stepped\par in. The government is not against a weaker Singapore dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par They just want to moderate the pace of the depreciation,"\par said a trader at a Japanese bank in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    The MAS declined to confirm the specific \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par but a spokesman did say that "as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's fundamentals\par remain sound, we see no reason why the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar\par should weaken."\par    Traders said that the MAS had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  consistently\par throughout the day, one estimating that the authority had\par sold as much as $200 million in U.S. dollars in the action.\par One trader at a U.S. bank suggested that the MAS intends to\par force the Singapore dollar temporarily higher in order to\par punish market participants with short positions, by forcing\par them to book losses in the run-up to the year's end.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS  12-17-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0705EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4340 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dtch02tk9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
