\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah slips to new low of 3,940 vs dlr. \b0\par\par\uc2 350 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Dec 3 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah slipped to a new low of 3,940 against the dollar on Wednesday as sentiment across the region was in the doldrums, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the low for the rupiah was 3,940 in Singapore and 3,935 in Jakarta. Spot rupiah was at 3,938/48 at 0515 GMT, compared with an opening of 3,800/15. The previous low for the rupiah was 3,865 on October 6. \par \par \uc2  The dealers said the market was likely to test the 4,000 barrier if the 3,950 level was broken. \par \par \uc2  "If that happens, I think the rupiah is going to overshoot again because of stop-loss selling," one chief treasurer said. \par \par \uc2  He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen checking one-week swap prices, but had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  yet. Dealers said cheap swaps at the short-end had also made long dollar holdings attractive. \par \par \uc2  They said the market was very thin, which favoured the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepping in. They, however, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to be reluctant because of a slump in the region. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said operators were also seen buying dollars following comments by Finance Minister Mar'ie Muhammad in Malaysia that concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Indonesia, \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Japan had been put on hold because the entire region was in a slump. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the underlying tone remained weak for the rupiah and for \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah ended firmer in New York overnight at 3,800/10 and the more positive tone extended to the opening in Jakarta before falling afoul of regional woes. \par \par \uc2  One Japanese bank dealer said the market was so thin that people only needed small volumes to move the whole market. \par \par \uc2  One Singapore-based dealer said he was worried about entering the market at current levels because the rupiah appeared to be oversold. However, the whole region was in a slump, he added. \par \par \uc2  -- Jakarta newsroom (6221) 384-6364; Fax (6221) 344-8404 \par \par \uc2  -- E-mail: jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtc301i7l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
