\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore dollar sinks to low of 1.5900/20. \b0\par\par\uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Nov 18 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar sank to a low of 1.5900/20 to the U.S. dollar in late morning trade on Tuesday after Singapore's senior minister Lee Kuan Yew said the level of the local dollar was a matter for the markets to decide. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Singapore dollar was also battered by keen selling of the ringgit/Sing by U.S. players. \par \par \uc2  "Lee's comments made some impact but the Singapore dollar also weakened because of the Kuala Lumpur stock market is bad. Some U.S. players are selling the ringgit/Sing," said a dealer with a local bank. \par \par \uc2  At 0345 GMT, Malaysia's key composite stock market index was down 5.74 percent at 628.99. \par \par \uc2  In an interview with Reuters, Lee said the relative strength of the Singapore dollar, which has fallen far less against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  than some other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , would have a negative impact. \par \par \uc2  "That's going to be a real problem for us because they are much cheaper than us now...they have gone down by 25 to 35 to, in the case of the Thai baht, about 40 percent against the U.S. dollar and we've only gone down barely 10 percent," Lee said. \par \par \uc2  But he said the level of the Singapore dollar against the other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a matter for the markets to decide. \par \par \uc2  At 0345 GMT, the Singapore dollar was quoted around 1.5890/10. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they were watching to see if Singapore's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS), which had been absent so far, would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  later. \par \par \uc2  -- Angela Tan (65) 870-3083; Fax (65) 776-8112 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: singapore.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtbi02cd5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
