\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 : Focus Still On Rupiah,  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By Roger Malone \par \uc2 240 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 1997\par 12:11\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (Dow Jones)--Attention in Southeast Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market focused again Friday on the Indonesia rupiah\par and talk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Bank Indonesia.\par    Traders said the amount spent to support the Indonesian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Friday was likely very small, but they noted in\par current thin markets, that might be enough for a temporary\par fix.\par    "The market is really quiet at the moment, so any big\par buying will move the market," said one Singapore-based\par trader for a U.S. bank. "It (the rupiah's move) stopped, but\par it's still rather high."\par    Late in the Asian trading day, the Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was heard selling dollars at 3,450 rupiah. There was no\par confirmation of the move.\par    After trading as high as 3,475 rupiah during Asian\par trading, the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dropped below 3,450 rupiah\par following the rumored \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and settled at 3,433.50\par late in Asia. The dollar was at 3,400 late Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Also helping the rupiah Friday was talk that the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore, the city-state's de facto\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was checking dollar rates against the rupiah.\par MAS officials weren't available for comment.\par    Rumors abounded in Indonesia Friday. Among them were the\par death of an influential banker and the closing of a\par Indonesian bank's Singapore branch - both proved false.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS  11-14-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0611EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4340 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dtbe02g52\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
