\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Slip Despite Bank Indonesia  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By Tom Holland \par \uc2 275 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 1997\par 12:36\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (Dow Jones)--Bank Indonesia again \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market on Thursday in an attempt to\par put the brakes on the rupiah's fall against the U.S. dollar.\par The Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's action lacked the aggression\par of the previous week's concerted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , however, and\par proved insufficient in steadying the ailing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par    With regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets largely\par discounting highly favorable comments by International\par Monetary Fund Managing Director Michel Camdessus about\par Indonesia and Thailand, other Southeast Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par also slipped lower against the U.S. dollar.\par    The Thai baht, the Malaysian ringgit and the Singapore\par dollar all finished Asian trading down from the previous\par day, but according to regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traders market\par activity was sparse and lacking any definite trend.\par    U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  dollar purchases against the rupiah in overnight\par trading prompted Bank Indonesia to enter the market early\par Thursday, after the Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  opened in Asia below\par the 4,000 rupiah to the U.S. dollar level.\par    Moderate sales of U.S. dollars from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par were sufficient to boost the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  back up to 3,365\par rupiah to the U.S. dollar, but U.S. dollar-buying interest\par soon re-emerged, said traders.\par    "The market is still looking for another run on the\par rupiah," said a regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader at a U.K. bank in\par Singapore. "There will have to be a turnaround in sentiment\par before we see any recovery, and that has not happened yet.\par Right now nothing has changed - Indonesia still has a\par serious structural problem."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS  11-13-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0636EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4340 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dtbd02fj5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
