\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mixed Early; Mkt Nervous Of  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 267 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 November 1997\par 03:14\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (DOW JONES)--Southeast Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are\par mixed in early trading Friday, with the Indonesian rupiah\par and Singapore dollar both lower against the U.S. dollar,\par while the Malaysian ringgit and the Thai baht are up from\par levels seen late Thursday.\par    Activity in the market is subdued, with traders saying\par the only notable order flow consists of sales of U.S.\par dollars against the Thai baht, sourced largely from Hong\par Kong.\par    While the overall sentiment toward regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par is still negative, market participants are hanging back,\par nervous of further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  action following the\par concerted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of recent days.\par    At 0200 GMT (9 p.m. Thursday EST) the U.S. dollar is\par quoted at 3,310 rupiah, up from 3,280 rupiah late Thursday,\par and "approaching the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  zone," according to one\par trader at a U.S. bank in Singapore.\par    Against the Singapore dollar, the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is at\par S$1.5755, up from S$1.5690 late Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Although the market is looking for the Singapore dollar\par to drop further, in line with other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , in\par the short term its fall is due to commercial interest to\par sell U.S. dollars, traders say.\par    At the same time the U.S. dollar is at 3.3147 ringgit,\par down a touch from 3.3150 late the previous day.\par    Against the Thai \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  the U.S. dollar is trading at\par 38.95 baht in the offshore market, below 39.3650 baht at the\par close of Asian trading Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS  11-06-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2114EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4340 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dtb702dwq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
