\par\par \b \uc2  PRESS DIGEST - Singapore - November 7. \b0\par\par\uc2 361 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Nov 7 (Reuters) - Following are the top stories from selected Singapore newspapers. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy. \par \par \uc2  THE STRAITS TIMES: \par \par \uc2  -  Court of Appeal upholds Chief Justice judgement in landmark Official Secrets Act case, imposing tighter standards for Act's use, and dismisses arguments put forward by Attorney-General. \par \par \uc2  -  After day of intense political horse-trading, Democrat Party leader Chuan Leekpai appears on course to form next Thai government and replace General Chavalit Yongchaiyudh, whose resignation as Prime Minister took effect on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -  King Bhumibol Adulyadej admitted to hospital for medical examination after developed irregular heartbeat. \par \par \uc2  -  \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  second time this week to support Indonesian rupiah, move that lends some strength to Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  buffeted by fears economic contagion could be knocking on South Korea door. \par \par \uc2  -  Top bids for private housing land in latest state sale have fallen back to early 1994 levels, say analysts. \par \par \uc2  -  Number and value of shares traded on Stock Exchange of Singapore in first 10 months exceeded last year's total turnover, as result of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  turmoil in last four months. \par \par \uc2  THE BUSINESS TIMES: \par \par \uc2  -  Developers bid between 25 and 30 percent below expectations for well-located residential site in Queenstown in latest land tender. \par \par \uc2  -  International Monetary Fund announces tough target for Jakarta to meet under US$33 billion three-year plan. \par \par \uc2  -  After arduous year whipping company back into shape and seeing Creative Technology stock breaching S$40 level, entrepreneur Sim Wong Hoo's market worth tops S$1 billion. \par \par \uc2  -  Overseas Union Bank eight billion yen exposure to collapsed Sanyo Securities group is well-covered, says bank. \par \par \uc2  -  Greenback rise against Singapore dollar will not have significant long-term impact on Neptune Orient Lines purchase cost for U.S.-shipping company American President Lines. \par \par \uc2  -  Tan Chong Motor Holdings to initially lease out maiden condo project, Wilby Residence, rather than sell, in view of soft market, say sources. \par \par \uc2  -  Stock Exchange of Singapore approves Japanese software manufacturer Konami Co proposed secondary listing on mainboard. \par \par \uc2  -- Singapore Newsroom (65) 870-3080; Fax (65) 776-8112 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: singapore.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtb702tt7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
