\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Central banks act again to help rupiah. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sonali Desai \par \uc2 974 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Nov 6 (Reuters) - Talk of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the Indonesian rupiah helped most Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  recoup early losses on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  reversed track after the Indonesian rupiah jumped to around 3,260 to the dollar from its lows of 3,330 in afternoon trade. \par \par \uc2  The move triggered strong speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS) had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy rupiah with Bank Indonesia in a move similar to Monday's joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  which also included the Bank of Japan (BOJ). \par \par \uc2  The MAS later confirmed it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in concert with Bank Indonesia and the BOJ, but gave no further details. \par \par \uc2  Dealers were unsure of the amount of the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but they said the market remained on edge for further such moves amid vague rumours that Malaysia and Brunei had also been involved in the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It was kind of a sudden move. One minute dollar/rupiah was at 3,340, the next minute it was at 3,260...when the central banks hit the market, the next move was very fast," said Ishak Ismail, market intelligence analyst at I.D.E.A. \par \par \uc2  "Normally, Bank Indonesia comes in in excess of $80-$100 million. But the MAS could have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a bigger amount because the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is large," he said. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, Singapore Finance Minister Richard Hu and Japanese Finance Hiroshi Mitsuzuka said the day's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was aimed at correcting what they called the excessive depreciation of the rupiah and they would act again if needed. \par \par \uc2  Traders estimated the three central banks sold between $300 million and $500 million on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was at 3,280/90 to the dollar at 1030 GMT on Tuesday against 3,330/40 six hours earlier. \par \par \uc2  "There are dollar bids coming in around 3,270/80, but it depends on their intentions. If they want to really push the dollar lower, they could come in again," a U.S. bank dealer in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian ringgit was also near its day highs at 3.2950/50 to the dollar against 3.3200/300 earlier. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Bank Negara's agent banks were selling dollars for ringgit, sparking speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was taking advantage of the dollar's downturn against regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shore up the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The ringgit had weakened earlier on news Kuala Lumpur had approved a start next year to work on a 10 billion ringgit landbridge with Thailand, raising questions about Malaysia's commitment to cutting its current account deficit. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar popped above 1.5700 to the U.S. dollar on rumours oil-rich Brunei was selling U.S. dollars above that level. But it slid back to 1.5720/40 by 1030 GMT, little changed from its midday levels. \par \par \uc2  Even the Thai baht firmed to 38.70/39.00 per dollar onshore but remained weak offshore at 39.30/60 as players awaited the outcome of talks between political parties to choose a successor to outgoing Prime Minister Chavalit Yongchaiyudh. \par \par \uc2  Former prime ministers Chuan Leekpai and Chatichai Choonhavan were touted as front-runners for the post, but conflicting Thai media reports left the market reluctant to act. \par \par \uc2  "At the moment, nobody even knows who the actual prime minister is," the head of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a European bank in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  Bangkok dealers said the baht was receiving some support from exporters on a belief that it would strengthen if Chuan, leader of the Democrat Party, became prime minister. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the health of 69-year-old King Bhumibol Adulyadej also remained a source of concern. \par \par \uc2  "If something happens to the King, that will undermine investor confidence again. He's the only one who can have some impact on the political scene," the Singapore dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso ended weak at 34.830 to the dollar against Wednesday's 34.74 close as sentiment soured after the Supreme Court declared oil deregulation unconstitutional. \par \par \uc2  The Korean won ended weak at 975.00 to the dollar against Wednesday's 969.7, despite repeated dollar sales by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reassurances by officials. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's failure to defend the 970.00 won level, previously a trigger-point for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , earlier sparked rumours overseas of an impending devaluation, causing the won to weaken in the non-deliverable forwards market. \par \par \uc2  But an official at the Bank of Korea strongly denied the rumours, saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's "will to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is as firm as ever". \par \par \uc2  A senior Finance Ministry official also denied talk that South Korea would seek emergency loans from the International Monetary Fund (IMF). \par \par \uc2  "Our financial markets are not in serious danger. We have no plan to request emergency loans from the IMF," said Choi Joong-kyong, director-general of the ministry's financial cooperation division. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar was steady at 7.7315/25 per U.S. dollar, paring its early gains, but dealers said fears of another speculative attack on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mounting as forwards firmed, pushing interest rates up. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong Chief Executive Tung Chee-hwa said he expected interest rates to fall once the government succeeded in defending the local dollar's peg to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  He said the government's policy of defending the peg "will never change". \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar ended lower at T$30.700 from Wednesday's T$30.451 close, under pressure from the U.S. dollar's overnight surge to six-month highs against the yen. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar lost more than half a cent after the Reserve Bank governor Ian Macfarlane highlighted the dangers financial strife in Asia held for exports. It was at $0.6991/96 from an early $0.7035/40. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011004dtb600msg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
