\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS - Korean won woes weigh on Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sonali Desai \par \uc2 933 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 1997\par 05:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Nov 6 (Reuters) - Worries about a possible devaluation of the Korean won, Thailand's political troubles and the illness of its king and Indonesia's long road to economic recovery depressed Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar's rise to six-month highs against the yen worsened the plight of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but dealers said there was no sign of panic selling and many institutions were winding down for the year-end. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won fell through the 970 level to the dollar, previously a trigger-point for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support, sparking rumours overseas of an impending devaluation. \par \par \uc2  But a Bank of Korea official said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had no plans to devalue the won or widen its 2.25 percent trading band. "Our will to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is as firm as ever," the official said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars at 975 won, cushioning further declines in the won for the time being. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar will trade mostly under 975 won level, but if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar could rise to 980 won," a dealer in Seoul said. The won was at 975.30/5.30 at 0445 GMT against Wednesday's close at 969.70. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said the bank did not concentrate exclusively on maintaining one level for its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "Watching the dollar/yen movement and adjusting our markets accordingly is important for stability as well." \par \par \uc2  Korea's dwindling foreign reserves and stricken financial sector have triggered growing speculation it might need to seek help from the International Monetary Fund (IMF). \par \par \uc2  In Thailand, the baht lost its footing as the market awaited the outcome of talks between political parties to choose a successor to outgoing Prime Minister Chavalit Yongchaiyudh. \par \par \uc2  Former prime ministers Chuan Leekpai and Chatichai Choonhavan are touted as front-runners for the post, but conflicting Thai media reports left the market reluctant to act. \par \par \uc2  "At the moment, nobody even knows who the actual prime minister is," the head of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a European bank in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  Bangkok dealers said the baht was receiving some support from exporters on a belief that it would strengthen if Chuan, leader of the Democrat Party, became prime minister. \par \par \uc2  The baht was at 39.10/20 to the dollar onshore against 38.90/39.20 late on Wednesday. Offshore baht was at 39.20/40 against 39.00/25. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the health of 69-year-old King Bhumibol Adulyadej also remained a source of concern. \par \par \uc2  "If something happens to the King, that will undermine investor confidence again. He's the only one who can have some impact on the political scene," the Singapore dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah slipped to 3,330/40 to the dollar from 3,300/10 late on Wednesday, but dealers said activity was confined to a narrow range between dollar demand and fears of aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The market seems stuck with short-covering at the 3,330 level from Singapore and selling interest from Jakarta at the 3,340 level," a U.S. bank dealer in Jakarta said. \par \par \uc2  Singapore dealers said players were having trouble pushing the dollar above the 3,400 rupiah level due to fears of a repeat of Monday's coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by Japan, \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  The IMF's approval of a $10 billion loan package as part of a massive international bailout for Indonesia had no impact. \par \par \uc2  IMF Managing Director Michel Camdessus praised Jakarta's efforts to reform the economy, but said slower growth and higher inflation would be unavoidable over the next two years. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian ringgit weakened to 3.3200/300 to the dollar from 3.2750/850 late Wednesday on news Kuala Lumpur had approved a start next year to work on a 10 billion ringgit landbridge with Thailand. \par \par \uc2  "The market is asking how serious is Malaysia in trying to cap its current account deficit. This kind of news certainly doesn't help," a dealer with a European bank in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  The government recently announced a delay in several large infrastructure and construction projects in a move to slow down the economy and cut the current account deficit. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar looked soft but was off its lows of 1.5795 to the U.S. dollar on a flight-to-quality from Thailand. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said it was likely to weaken again alongside its neighbours, with forwards seen moving to the right. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso recovered a bit after falling through the 35 to the dollar level in early trade, but dealers said sentiment remained poor after the Supreme Court's decision to declare oil deregulation unconstitutional. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar firmed to 7.7300/20 from 7.7325/35 on Wednesday as the wide interest rate spread with the U.S. dollar attracted players seeking a higher yield. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong Chief Executive Tung Chee-hwa said he expected interest rates to fall once the government succeeded in defending the local dollar's peg to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  He said the government's policy of defending the peg "will never change". \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong interest rates have risen in recent months as investors positioned for a possible attack on the peg and the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved to discourage speculation. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar eased to T$30.640/710 from Wednesday's T$30.451 close, under pressure from the U.S. dollar's overnight surge against the yen. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtb6033yu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
