\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mixed; Buying In Rupiah, Baht Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 292 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 1997\par 02:30\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Southeast Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are\par mixed against the the U.S. dollar early Tuesday compared\par with levels late Monday with buying seen in the rupiah and\par the baht and selling seen in the Singapore dollar and the\par ringgit.\par    Higher short term interest rates and the positive\par sentiment arising from the the International Monetary Fund\par package over the weekend to Indonesia are seen as key\par factors giving the rupiah a mild boost against the dollar.\par    Also, the decision by Thai Prime Minister Chavalit\par Yongchaiyudh to step down has boosted sentiment in the baht,\par said market players.\par    On the other hand, market players are selling Singapore\par dollars and the Malaysian ringgit against the dollar in an\par effort to push the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to levels seen in late\par Asian trading Monday. The Singapore dollar and ringgit\par strengthened in New York late Monday.\par    At 0110 GMT, the dollar is at 3,213 rupiah, down from\par 3,235 rupiah late Monday while it is at 39.15 baht, lower\par from 39.65 baht.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  The dollar is also at S$1.5480, up from\par S$1.5435 late Monday and is at 3.2500 ringgit, up from\par 3.2400 ringgit late Monday.\par    "People are looking at the rupiah very intensely today.\par Higher short term rates running at over 100% and the\par (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  yesterday are\par (seen) causing some firmness in the rupiah today," said the\par regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  head at a Japanese bank in Singapore.\par    "There are a lot of orders to buys the dollar at 3,200\par rupiah. The government is probably hoping that these buy\par orders will disappear soon," said the dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS  11-03-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2030EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4340 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dtb402cnt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
