\par\par \b \uc2  INTERVIEW- Nicholas-Applegate sees more Asia pain. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sonali Desai \par \uc2 547 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Nov 4 (Reuters) - Shaky Southeast Asian financial markets are likely to face more pain in the months ahead as their economies get on the road to difficult but much-needed reform, a fund manager said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Kim Teo, managing director of Nicholas-Applegate Capital Management Asia, said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock markets were enjoying a technical recovery, but the worst was not over. \par \par \uc2  "We think the reaction we are seeing in the markets is more a technical bounce from an oversold position," Teo told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  Japan and \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Monday to support the Indonesian rupiah with Bank Indonesia helped to calm nerves. \par \par \uc2  But Teo said there were more rocky times ahead as Indonesia and Thailand moved to restructure their economies to meet the International Monetary Fund's (IMF) conditions for assistance. \par \par \uc2  "The medicine has been paid for but it has to be taken, which means there will be further pain ahead," Teo said. \par \par \uc2  The IMF arranged a US$17.2 billion international loan package for Thailand in August and announced a US$23 billion multilateral aid package for Indonesia last week. \par \par \uc2  Teo said the Indonesian economy was unlikely to achieve the government's target of five to six percent economic growth this year. \par \par \uc2  "The restructuring itself would cause economic contraction to some extent...Perhaps we're looking at zero to two percent instead of five percent," he said. \par \par \uc2  Thai Prime Minister Chavalit Yongchaiyudh's announcement on Monday that he would resign had been well received by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, but it remained to be seen how his successor would cope with unpopular economic decisions, Teo said. \par \par \uc2  Singapore, which has been relatively cushioned from its neighbours' troubles, would see some impact on company earnings in the first quarter of next year, he said. \par \par \uc2  "Although Singapore is very well placed, there will still be a slowdown because of the hinterland that it services and the investments into the surrounding region which Singapore companies have been doing," Teo said. \par \par \uc2  He said the benchmark Straits Times Industrials stock index was unlikely to rally beyond the 1,800 points level. The index stood at 1,706.36 at 0821 GMT, up 0.14 percent. \par \par \uc2  Teo said Nicholas-Applegate was more bullish on North Asia, with the exception of South Korea. \par \par \uc2  He said the recent depreciation of the Taiwan dollar had been very helpful for the island's export industry. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar has slithered to 10-year lows of around T$31 to the U.S. dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  abandoned a watertight defence of the T$28.50 level on October 17. \par \par \uc2  "We're still optimistic on China and Hong Kong. We think the (Hong Kong dollar) peg will remain where it is," Teo said. \par \par \uc2  He said Hong Kong's blue chip Hang Seng Index was likely to head back for the 13,000 level after tumbling below 9,000 last week. \par \par \uc2  "(Asian) \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will remain weakish but certainly not at the near panic collapses we've seen. I think it will be a lot more orderly in the next one to three months." \par \par \uc2  -- Sonali Desai (65) 870-3090; Fax (65) 776-8112 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: singapore.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtb4037wr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
