\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  upbeat as baht revives. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jacqueline Wong \par \uc2 614 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 1997\par 06:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Nov 4 (Reuters) - An impressive early rally by the Thai baht after Prime Minister Chavalit Yongchaiyudh said he would resign boosted Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The markets reacted positively to the news, although early buying of the beleaguered baht cooled somewhat on uncertainties surrounding efforts to reform the economy, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "A lot of U.S. investment funds tried to push dollar/baht higher, but it seems there were very good offers around the 39.50 level," a dealer with a local bank said. \par \par \uc2  The baht was quoted at 39.20/30 per dollar in the onshore market against 40.90/41.00 late on Monday. Earlier, dollar/baht fell to 38.90 in a knee jerk reaction to Chavalit's resignation promise. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said, however, concerns on the political situation would cap gains in the short term. "The market is still not too confident that Thailand will have a quick recovery, like Indonesia," said one. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's efforts to reform its economy in response to a massive IMF-led aid package continued to lift the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the scramble caused by tighter liquidity after three central banks \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday to buy the rupiah lifted offshore and forward rates against the U.S dollar. \par \par \uc2  The value of concerted dollar sales for rupiah in Singapore on Monday by the Bank of Japan (BOJ), the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) and Bank Indonesia was estimated at $300 to $500 million, senior Japanese traders said. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah traded in a narrow range between 3,205 and 3,265 against the U.S. dollar with an upward bias firmly in place. At 0445 GMT, dollar/rupiah was at 3,215/00 against its New York close at 3,205. \par \par \uc2  Malaysia's ringgit came off its highs on profit taking after recent sharp rises with dollar/ringgit slipping to 3.2730 per U.S. dollar against 3.2600/700 earlier. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said selling was expected after the ringgit's recent bounce but that they saw a further test of the 3.20 per dollar resistance. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar drifted lower to 1.5588/90 with one dealer citing rumours of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying of dollars against the Sing below the 1.55 level. \par \par \uc2  Others said they had expected the Singapore dollar to rise after Japanese Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitzuzuka said that Monday's joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would bring \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability to Southeast Asia. \par \par \uc2  They felt \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , already in a more positive posture than other regionals, would make further gains. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar was slightly weaker at 7.7360/70 against the U.S. dollar, but forwards firmed in line with regional forwards like the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  The interbank rate was slightly higher at Tuesday's fixing, while overnight rates also climbed, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso rose to 34.70 against the U.S. dollar compared with 35.10/20 on Monday. Rates hit a high of 34.55 and a low of 34.95, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  pegging its selling price at 34.85/90. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar climbed on profit taking on the  U.S. dollar. Comments from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that Taiwan's dollar had already lost too much value also helped its recovery to T$30.737 against Monday's T$31.245. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won traded at 958.00/000, underpinned by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's determination to curb rises in the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Korea poured about $300 million into the market to support the local unit, dealers said. The bank sold dollars at 970 won in spot trading early. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtb4037qr\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (Singapore near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\br